00:33:41.410 --> 00:33:44.870
- It should do well with the plastic cast, I think.

00:33:44.870 --> 00:33:46.270
- You think? - No, I know.

00:33:46.270 --> 00:33:48.430
- You're not going to use a splint?

00:33:48.430 --> 00:33:50.550
- The plastic cast should be sufficient

00:33:50.550 --> 00:33:51.430
to hold it in alignment.

00:33:51.430 --> 00:33:52.090
- Should?

00:33:52.090 --> 00:33:56.200
- It will be.

00:33:56.200 --> 00:33:57.270
- Very good, carry on.

00:34:01.560 --> 00:34:05.060
Don't worry. We're here now.

00:34:05.060 --> 00:34:07.110
We're going to look after.

00:34:07.110 --> 00:34:20.290
I'll be back to see you soon.

00:34:20.290 --> 00:34:22.080
To see the calf.

00:34:22.080 --> 00:34:24.140
To remove the calf from its leg.

00:34:24.140 --> 00:34:25.700
In a couple of months.

00:34:25.700 --> 00:34:26.340
Weeks.

00:34:26.340 --> 00:34:29.190
I better go.

00:34:30.120 --> 00:34:31.000
It was nice meeting you.

00:34:31.000 --> 00:34:31.890
You too.

00:34:31.890 --> 00:34:33.110
Wait, James.

00:34:33.110 --> 00:34:37.910
Siegfried's bark really is worse than his bite.

00:34:37.910 --> 00:34:39.860
He's been very kind to us.

00:34:39.860 --> 00:34:42.270
Underneath it all, he's a good man.

00:34:42.270 --> 00:34:46.000
Stand up to him.

00:34:46.000 --> 00:34:47.670
He'll love you for it.

00:34:47.670 --> 00:34:53.590
Chop, chop.

00:35:07.450 --> 00:35:09.250
